        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: argūmentum, argūmentī",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "argūmentum, argūmentī — \"an argument, a proof; a plot\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Hoc argūmentum mihi nōn persuādet. This argument does not persuade me."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "argūmentum, argūmentī n. It is also the plot of a play. Built on arguō, to make clear. English argument."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "argūmentum is built on arguō \"to make clear, to prove\" (EtymDB; Lewis & Short), with the ending -mentum that names a means. English argument comes from it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
