              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "cōnfirmō, cōnfirmāre — \"to strengthen; to confirm, to assert\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Litterae tuae opīniōnem meam cōnfirmant. Your letter confirms my opinion."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "cōnfirmō, cōnfirmāre, cōnfirmāvī, cōnfirmātum. Built on firmus, firm: to make firm, then to state firmly. Animum cōnfirmāre, to give someone courage. English confirm."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "cōnfirmō is built from con- and a verb made on firmus \"firm, strong\" (EtymDB; Lewis & Short): to make thoroughly firm. English confirm comes from it."
            }
          ]
        },
